From: iOSPlus10 ios26 port
Subject: [PATCH 0004] NEGRONI platform expert, boot CPU/SMP driver, framebuffer console, IOKit start

- iokit/Kernel/arm/NegroniPlatformExpert.cpp (slop 0016; ours 0211/0213 halt/restart hook), NegroniCPU.cpp
  (slop 0018, 0065, 0078: PSCI CPU_ON, 8 cores), KernelConfigTables.cpp + iokit/conf/files.arm64 (these two only;
  each driver patch adds its own personality and file line)
- pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c: framebuffer "serial" console from the ADT node negroni-fbcon (slop 0003, 0088);
  12377 serial_init looks for a /chosen serial phandle, so fbcon_probe() runs before that lookup
- osfmk/console/serial_console.c: persistent-log tee and console mute (slop 0043, 0047, 0067)
- osfmk/kern/debug.c: panic hooks (ours 0360, 0367)
- iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp, IOService.cpp: no 30 s IORTC wait (ours 0200), no kernelmanagerd busy hold
- osfmk/kern/negroni_top.c (ours 0382)
- osfmk/arm64/negroni_weak_hooks.c (new for 12377): weak default definitions of the driver hooks that the
  machine layer, console and platform expert call (log append, reboot/power off, RTC, RPMh sleep, panic hooks).
  The drivers give the strong definitions. So 0001-0004 link and boot to the console without bsd/dev drivers.

